  "about": "The Hollow Cairn's inside in Year 1 (Book 9 section 09, \"In Year 1\"; Stage 14, decisions S14-3, S14-10, S14-22 and S14-44): an interior of 48 x 30 tiles read tile for tile from docs/levels/hollow_cairn_tiles.txt by src/tools/levels/zones.ts, with no warp, as it is before anyone digs: Gróa's shaft (`g`) is rock and its rubble floor, the sea-light's places are floor, the great chamber is whole and dry. Its walls are drystone (`d`) along the floor and rock beyond; the floor dry earth (`:`); the spring's channel fresh water (`w`); the tidal passage to Seal Cave wet rock open only on spring lows (`n`), meeting the deep passage at its east edge. The Door of Three Truths is closed and blocks (`d`, its prop drawn), so the outer passage and the great chamber (by the east door) never meet the inner chamber and the spring room (by the tidal passage). The east door is a portal to the cairn's mound, open once cairn.door.open holds. Grave goods are looked at, not taken (their props). Edit this plan, not the generated map, then run npm run zones.",
